===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[subject#Verb|subject]] to the process of [[acclimation]].
#: {{ux|en|I became '''conditioned''' to the absence of seasons in San Diego.}}
# To subject to different conditions, especially as an exercise.
#: {{ux|en|They were '''conditioning''' their shins in their karate class.}}
# To make [[dependent]] on a condition to be fulfilled; to make [[conditional]] on. <!-- Oxford English Dictionary, sense 3: "To subject to something as a condition; to make dependent on a condition to be fulfilled; to make conditional on, upon." The first part is covered in the previous sense here. -->
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To place conditions or [[limitation]]s upon.
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Poems 1842|edition=4th|volume=II|poem=The Golden Year|page=89|passage=Yet seas that daily gain upon the shore / Have ebb and flow '''conditioning''' their march, / And slow and sure comes up the golden year.}}
# To [[shape#Verb|shape]] the [[behavior|behaviour]] of someone to do something.
#: {{ux|en|The children were '''conditioned''' to speak up if they had any disagreements.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To treat (the hair) with [[hair conditioner]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[contract]]; to [[stipulate]]; to [[agree]].
#* {{RQ:Beaumont Fletcher Comedies and Tragedies|folio=2nd|part=2|title=The Night Walker|act=II|scene=viii|page=212|column=2|passage=[P]ay me back my credit, / And I'll '''condition''' wi'ye.}}
